{"reasoning":"We minimize f(x)=1/2 x^T P x + q^T x with P=[[13,-14],[-14,17]], q=[-2,4], subject to 4x1+x2=5 and the inequalities 4x1-x2<=4, -4x1+4x2<=3. From the equality, x2=5-4x1. Substitute into the objective. First compute the quadratic part: x^T P x = 13x1^2 -28x1x2 +17x2^2. With x2=5-4x1, this becomes 13x1^2 -28x1(5-4x1)+17(5-4x1)^2 = 13x1^2 -140x1 +112x1^2 +425 -680x1 +272x1^2 = 397x1^2 -820x1 +425. So 1/2 x^T P x = 198.5 x1^2 -410x1 +212.5. Also q^T x = -2x1 +4(5-4x1)=20-18x1. Hence f(x)=198.5 x1^2 -428x1 +232.5.

Now the constraints in x1: 4x1-(5-4x1)<=4 gives 8x1<=9, so x1<=9/8. And -4x1+4(5-4x1)<=3 gives 20-20x1<=3, so x1>=17/20. Thus x1 in [0.85,1.125]. The unconstrained minimizer of the parabola is x1=428/(2*198.5)=428/397≈1.0781, which lies in the feasible interval, so it is optimal.

Evaluate f at x1=428/397. Using vertex formula, minimum value = 232.5 - 428^2/(4*198.5). Since 4*198.5=794, 428^2=183184, giving 232.5 - 183184/794 ≈ 232.5 - 230.7103 = 1.7897. So the optimal value is about 1.79.","answer":1.79}
